Sample Input: person_1 table with one row Sample Output: Error Code: 1292. Incorrect date value: '1996-09-45' for column 'dob' at row 1 A month cannot have a 45th day, so the DATE type rejects the value. Q13. Does a data type guarantee that the stored value is realistic? Show with an example. Ans: No. A data type only controls the kind of value. A column declared INT accepts any integer, even a negative weight or a weight of 1 kg, which no real person can have.

```java
INSERT INTO person_1 VALUES (2, 'Rahul', '2006-09-15', 'Calcutta', -45);
INSERT INTO person_1 VALUES (3, 'Amish', '1999-03-10', 'Mysuru', 1);
```

